# ghal_bol_core owns product logic

**`ghal_bol_core` (Rust)** owns crypto, P2P, outbox, acks, contacts, transcripts, invites, OS network truth, and coord/bridge policy.

**`ghal_bol_app` (Makepad 2)** is the only UI. It links `ghal_bol_core` and calls **`ghal_bol_core::host`** in-process. Splash is `script_mod!`. Where Makepad 2 lacks a widget or platform affordance, complete the behaviour in Splash. See `docs/MAKEPAD_UI.md`.

When adding features (including connectivity, acks, storage):

- Implement behaviour in **`ghal_bol_core`** and call it from **`ghal_bol_core::host`**.
- Keep the UI in-process via `host` — do not add a second language binding or out-of-process RPC for the Makepad app.
- The Makepad app polls and displays native state. Do not duplicate OS probes in the UI.
- Do not move ack policy, outbox, transcript merge, or WAN/LAN dial policy into Splash.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` for the full split.
